          "id": "the_thirty_year_fold_is_a_causal_self_reference",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §2.2(e), §6.0 and §6.1 step 3, at the four places the fold can go wrong without the answer looking wrong. It is a control on the construct of esm-spec §4.3.1.1 as much as on this chain: a recurrence that silently resolves an unpublished self-read to 0 produces plausible numbers for a whole axis, so every value here is a specific number and none is a bound.\n\nROW 31 IS 2020. Two equations index the last fold row as the literal 31; if `fold_year_rows` or `baseYearID` ever moved, this assertion is what fails instead of the fold quietly reading the wrong year.\n\nTHE FIRST STEP IS HAND-CHECKABLE. Row 2 is 1991, one growth step: totpop is 83.3 x (1 + 0.401523) = 116.74687, the minuend is that over 83.3 = 1.401523, and the scrapped sum is the whole of the 1990 newest cohort shifted one year and scrapped once, 0.8506725 x 0.265 = 0.22542821 -- the age-2 survival, the only non-zero factor in the vector at that point. The residual is the difference, 1.1760948. A fold that reassociated the year loop, or applied the survival before the shift, misses this at the first step.\n\nTHE LAST MINUEND IS THE GROWTH RATIO. Row 31's minuend is 4.6978183, which is G(2020)/G(1990) from §6.0 reached by thirty multiplications rather than by one division -- the check that the fold ran the right number of years, and in binary32 it agrees with the single division to 3e-07. This document now evaluates in binary32 (`domain.element_type`), so this test carries the 2^-23 tolerance docs/esm-conventions.md §17.4 fixes for a test whose every assertion is a floating-point quantity: the expected values stay the specification's decimals and the tolerance moves, never the other way round.",
