        {
          "id": "the_fold_reproduces_the_second_worked_example_hp_5_5_point",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.2, 'Derived per point', the 5.5 hp equipment point of SCC 2265007015: 200 full-load hours at 350 hours a year gives medianLifeYears 0.8163266 and nyrlif 3, and the fold of its base population 1.1 gives modfrc (3.9099162, 0.7879026, 0.0). The third slot is EXACTLY zero, not a residue: age 3 has yryrfrcscrp = 1 here, so the shift zeroes the cohort and prccty.f's `modfrc <= 0` skip drops the model year. That is the same skip §7.3 shows removing 44 cohorts across the fixture, exercised on a point where it is checkable by hand -- and it is the counterpart of §6.1's 5.9e-08, which the same predicate KEEPS. This document now evaluates in binary32 (`domain.element_type`), so this test carries the 2^-23 tolerance docs/esm-conventions.md §17.4 fixes for a test whose every assertion is a floating-point quantity: the expected values stay the specification's decimals and the tolerance moves, never the other way round.",
