          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.2, the 9.0 hp point of the same SCC: 400 full-load hours at 350 hours a year, nyrlif 5, base population 0.5, modfrc (2.1914759, 2.0018263, 0.4327385, 0.0717785, 0.0). Five slots rather than three, so the fold's longer lags are exercised: slot 5 reads a residual five years back, and every slot beyond the first reads a run of survival factors rather than one. §6.2 notes that this point's nyrlif would reach MY2016 and does not, because slot 5 is zero -- the assertion on that slot is that claim. This document now evaluates in binary32 (`domain.element_type`), so this test carries the 2^-23 tolerance docs/esm-conventions.md §17.4 fixes for a test whose every assertion is a floating-point quantity: the expected values stay the specification's decimals and the tolerance moves, never the other way round. ONE ASSERTION IS LOOSER, AND THE REFERENCE IS WHY. §6.2 prints `0.0717785` -- six significant figures, one fewer than the others in that table because of the leading zero -- and half an ulp of that print is 7.0e-07 relative, which is coarser than the 1.2e-07 binary32 epsilon the rest of this file is pinned at. The computed value is 0.07177852839231491, bit-identical to the float32 reproduction; what cannot resolve it is the printed decimal, so that one assertion carries the print's own resolution, 1e-06, and the others do not.",
